    "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/h4chub/kapkan-releases/tarball/v1.0.2-beta.1",
    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/h4chub/kapkan-releases/zipball/v1.0.2-beta.1",
    "body": "KapKan 1.0.2 adds update notices and includes the faster downloads from 1.0.1.\r\n\r\n## For people who already installed KapKan\r\n\r\n**Install 1.0.2 manually once.** The earlier 1.0.0 and 1.0.1 builds do not contain an update checker, so they cannot show this notice themselves.\r\n\r\nAfter that, KapKan checks for newer releases when it opens. An available update shows **Download update** and **Later**. There is also **Check for updates** in Settings. Startup checks are enabled by default and can be turned off.\r\n\r\nThe notice waits while Minecraft is preparing or running. Download update opens the correct official installer in your browser. You still close Minecraft and KapKan and install the download yourself; this release does not silently install updates.\r\n\r\n## Also included\r\n\r\n- Up to six Minecraft asset downloads at once, verified cache reuse and duplicate-content detection.\r\n- File progress, measured speed and estimated download time remaining.\r\n- Existing launcher design, in-game menu, capes and skin importer.\r\n- Verified older 1.0.1 Mac app copies can be retired by the existing cleanup feature. Worlds, mods, accounts and preferences stay in the data folder.\r\n\r\n## Download and install\r\n\r\n**macOS:** download `KapKan-macOS-1.0.2.zip`, close Minecraft and KapKan, extract it and move `KapKan.app` into Applications, replacing the old app.\r\n\r\n**Windows x64:** download `KapKan-1.0.2-Setup.exe`, close Minecraft and KapKan, then run the installer.\r\n\r\nKeep your existing `.kapkan` data directory. `SHA256SUMS.txt` identifies the exact downloads.\r\n\r\n## Beta scope\r\n\r\nThe in-game companion targets **Minecraft 26.1.2, Fabric Loader 0.19.5 or newer, and Java 25**. Other offered versions/loaders do not all have these features or completed compatibility testing.\r\n\r\nMicrosoft sign-in is not preconfigured with a KapKan-owned application ID. Shared badges/capes need a configured HTTPS service; none is included by default. Imported skins remain local. Friends, managed server creation and Premium are not available.\r\n\r\nThe packages are unsigned and macOS is not notarized. Update discovery/recovery fixtures, Linux Swing UI checks at 1x and 2x, retained regression tests and package audits passed. Native Mac/Windows installation, gameplay and live update discovery still need device confirmation. An offline connection or GitHub rate limit can delay update detection; Settings lets you retry.\r\n"
  },
