    "body": "KapKan’s first public beta brings the updated launcher and in-game cosmetics menu.\r\n\r\n## Included\r\n\r\n- Modern in-game menu with an unused key chosen automatically and shown in a fading welcome card.\r\n- Black, Ivory and Burgundy capes, cloth motion, colour customization and custom PNG importing.\r\n- White cape logos and name badges with consistent rendering in the world and menu.\r\n- Local skin importing, optional FPS/coordinate HUD and hold-to-zoom.\r\n- Cleaner launcher Running text and focus behaviour, plus a link to compatible cape downloads.\r\n- Existing worlds, mods, preferences and imported cosmetics are retained during a normal app update.\r\n\r\n## Download and update\r\n\r\n**macOS:** download `KapKan-macOS-1.0.0.zip`, close Minecraft and KapKan, extract it and move the included `KapKan.app` into Applications, replacing the old app.\r\n\r\n**Windows x64:** download `KapKan-1.0.0-Setup.exe`, close Minecraft and KapKan, then run the installer.\r\n\r\nThe first update is manual. This build does not contain an automatic launcher updater. Keep your `.kapkan` data directory. `SHA256SUMS.txt` identifies the exact downloadable files.\r\n\r\n## Beta scope\r\n\r\nThe new in-game companion targets **Minecraft 26.1.2, Fabric Loader 0.19.5 or newer, and Java 25**. Other versions/loaders offered by the launcher do not all have these features or completed compatibility testing.\r\n\r\nMicrosoft sign-in is not preconfigured with a KapKan-owned application ID. Shared badges/capes need a configured HTTPS service; no shared endpoint is included by default. Custom skins remain local. Friends, managed server creation and Premium are not available in this release.\r\n\r\nThese packages are unsigned; macOS is not Developer ID notarized. Minecraft and launcher runtime checks passed on Linux. Installation and gameplay on the exact Mac/Windows packages still need native confirmation. This is an early-access build."
